  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Freedom of Religion or Belief in India: A Study on the Need for Wider Dissemination</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Purpose
1. We wish to measure the level of knowledge related to FORB issues among different stakeholders to decide the degree of dissemination needed. 
2. We will test various methodologies (Focus Group Discussions (FGDs), Training, Seminar, Films, Panel discussions in public) for the dissemination of FoRB knowledge to different stakeholders. During this stage, we will also take notes on how much the content of the existing FoRB material resonates with community members, thereby determining if the content needs to be adapted.  

Participants will include common people, faith leaders, civil society activists, human rights defenders, local media.

Expected Outcome
1. Level of FoRB knowledge among key stakeholders established 
2. Methodologies for the dissemination of FoRB knowledge among different stakeholders for the Pilot Project tried and tested
3. Understanding the gaps in our teaching material, to make the teaching material relevant.</narrative>
  </description>
